 objective and clear mindset  i needed to dive into it  a little more and i think i was afraid  of doing that for a very long time  before i started writing sonia i was  kind of turning my eyes away from it  so that i didn't have to deal with it or  look it directly in the face  and when i did and i gave myself  a lot of time to to formulate my  thoughts on it  it uh it helped me come to peace with a  lot of it  and you know i finished writing for  example i finished  revising i should say the final episode  last week  so i'm still writing it and i still have  changes and  new things that i come to if it was up  to me  i'd probably be writing it the rest of  my life  i i just also know that it needs to get  out there at some point or another  i am so thrilled and excited about this  new project for you because you've been  working on this for  more than five years now um why  a comic book why have this be your next  avenue in your career  well yeah thank you um it's interesting  you know i started writing this  five years ago because i was kind of  in a place mentally where i felt like i  needed to get  some sort of story out for myself to  better understand the scenario that was  happening  and so i started writing something that  i just knew  i loved which was fantasy genre and i  thought that i could  kind of uh place the setting around  the idea in an interesting way so i  started writing it like that but i  actually  intended it to be live action um and  when i started writing it and intending  it to be live action i realized that it  was restricting me  from making it the way i envisioned it  because i was  in the back of my mind i was thinking  about things like budget and i was  thinking about  like how physically someone would even  do these things  um so i actually just changed gears  completely and i ended up writing it for  comics and for animation  um and i found that my thoughts were  much more free-flowing at that point  i was able to do things i wasn